+
+## Creating a JSON Patch
+
+`createPatch(from, to)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returns a JSON Patch (RFC 6902) that turns `from`
+into `to` when passed to `applyPatch`. It describes only what changed: unchanged members and array
+elements produce no operation, nested changes are addressed by their own path, and identical documents
+give an empty patch. Arrays keep their common head and tail, so inserting or deleting an element is one
+operation rather than a rewrite of the rest. Neither argument is mutated and the patch shares no
+structure with them. It throws an `Error` if `from` or `to` is not JSON (see `applyPatch`).
